 ## Facts (verified)
 
+- **2026-11-13, offline, JC303 sequencer 0.1.0:** optional weak engine hook
+  `mpc_engine_cycle(inst,start,end,active)` supplies valid loop endpoints before
+  song_pos(). VST2 requests cycle positions; VST3 uses ProcessContext cycle
+  fields. Missing timing calls song_pos with invalid position/stopped state.
+  Native ASan/UBSan and ARM64 QEMU tests compare exact audio to an independently
+  scheduled voice through a loop ending within a host block (maximum error 0),
+  and check tempo changes, jitter, gates, ties, project pattern state, record
+  and generator limits. This is not a device CPU or GUI verification.
+
+- **2026-11-12, offline JC303 0.0.3 regression:** accepted stepped-value feedback
+  introduced a second interaction: an exact host echo reset last_pos during a
+  fractional absolute sweep, making the next increasing value look decreasing.
+  VST2 now records the stepped values it reports and recognises matching host
+  acknowledgements without changing gesture history. Tests cover all six LFO
+  waves forward/backward, independent wheel clicks, synchronous and delayed
+  echoes, and ordinary exact touch writes. Native ASan/UBSan and ARM64 QEMU pass;
+  device confirmation is pending.
+
+- **2026-11-12, offline regression plus user report, JC303 Live III:** fractional VST2
+  Q-Link writes were settled to an exact option in the engine but never reported back
+  to the host. The host could retain e.g. 1/128 while a switch was already on, leaving
+  touchscreen buttons and radio selections stale. `set_param_now()` now queues
+  audioMasterAutomate for a stepped value it changes. Housekeeping reports the accepted
+  value outside setParameter; a host echo of the exact value queues no further report.
+  JC303's regression reproduces the stale cached host value before the fix and covers
+  MODS, filter, LFO wave/destination and feedback echoes after it. Hardware confirmation
+  of this correction is pending; the user's report concerns the previous build.
+
+- **2026-11-12, offline only, JC303 milestone 1:** `ENGINE_FLOAT32=1` selects interleaved float engine
+  buffers in both wrappers; existing ports keep int16. The engine includes generated `params.h` before
+  `engine.h`. Native VST2 tests under ASan/UBSan compared three JC303 filters against a direct voice
+  with an event at sample 37 and host blocks of 1–511 frames: maximum absolute error < 2e-9.
+  The existing int16 inputprobe host test also passes. No MPC hardware test or CPU claim.
+
