 ## 1. Engine
+- Host-synchronised engines may additionally implement the weak
+  `mpc_engine_cycle(inst,start,end,active)` hook. With `HAS_SONG_POS=1`, both
+  wrappers call it before `song_pos()` to describe a valid active host loop.
+  Use it to split a render block at a loop end; invalid/missing time stops the
+  clock through `song_pos(-1,0,0,frames)`. JC303's 0.1.0 host tests cover this
+  offline with an end inside a block; actual MPC verification is still required.
+- [ ] Optional float audio: `"defines": {"ENGINE_FLOAT32": 1}` selects interleaved `float` samples in
+      `mpc_engine_t.render/process` (`mpc_sample_t`, `wrapper/audio_format.h`), in VST2 and desktop VST3.
+      Include generated `params.h` before `engine.h` in the engine; all translation units must agree.
+      The default remains int16. Float keeps low-level precision and headroom; no int16 clipping is applied.
